Chronology has a separate new source boundary. Direct query payloads retain
composition/narrated-event relations, requested and resolved profiles, source
IDs, raw labels, dispositions and scopes. They are not patristic evidence and
must become fresh research before entering either published study.

Only the same-edition PC-S44-A pilot was read for layout/component precedent.
Its dated prose, older metadata wrappers, repeated-heading conventions and
cross-proper interpretations are not copied into this draft. The present
PC-S51-A accepted study remains the sole interpretive authority.
